				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1499,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Mountain): Fix invisible whitespace artifacts in section headers\n\nThe `Documentation/GitHub/Architecture.md` file contained invisible non-breaking space characters (U+00A0) between the header text and emojis in all major section titles. These artifacts caused inconsistent rendering and length discrepancies in Markdown viewers.\n\nStrip the non-breaking spaces and replace them with standard ASCII spaces in the title line and all H2/H3 headers (e.g., `Overview`, `Application Lifecycle`, `Module Architecture`, `Provider Registration`, `Tauri Command System`, `gRPC Service`, `Process Management`, `IPC and Event System`, `Cache System`, `Extension Management`, `Related Documentation`).\n\nThis restores visual consistency across the documentation and aligns with the project's formatting standards established in the recent commit `302e3fe`.",
			"SHA": "4495e6f1fc92b2213c73dce4d5473b634ef1435f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-15T23:36:50Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1499,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Mountain): Standardize documentation formatting and add component emojis\n\nRefactor the Architecture.md document to align with strict project formatting guidelines. Update inline code elements (e.g., `Tauri`, `Rust`, `gRPC`) and standardize emoji usage in section headers to ensure consistent rendering across Markdown viewers.\n\nEnhance the `Related Documentation` section by converting relative links to absolute GitHub URLs targeting the `Current` branch. Add a summary list of Mountain's core responsibilities at the introduction and apply a mountain emoji (🏔️) to the title. Update the `Process Management` and `Environment` sections to explicitly reference `PATH`, `SIGTERM`, and `AppState` with code formatting for clarity.\n\nThese changes improve document readability and maintain consistency with the project's documentation standards.",
			"SHA": "302e3fdea12b8e7084cf8a13ddeb4c67f72833c8"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-15T22:32:55Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1499,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Mountain): Add Mermaid sequence diagram for application lifecycle\n\nExpand the `Documentation/GitHub/Architecture.md` file by inserting a Mermaid sequence diagram that visualizes the Mountain startup process. The diagram details the initialization order from `main()`, through `Tauri::Builder` setup, `AppState` creation, and `MountainEnvironment` provider injection, to the spawning of background tasks.\n\nKey stages captured include the initialization of the Echo scheduler (`AppRuntime`), the launch of the gRPC server (Vine), the bootstrap handshake with the Cocoon extension host, and the optional connection to the Air daemon. This addition provides a clear, visual reference for the complex inter-process orchestration defined in the preceding text.",
			"SHA": "064ab84c283122d356b3418ecccd91a17be83326"
		}
